ment specifies editorial information that appears in footnotes in the printed score. It is defined within a group due to its multiple uses within the MusicXML schema."}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"name":"level","content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The level element specifies editorial information for different MusicXML elements. It is defined within a group due to its multiple uses within the MusicXML schema."}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"name":"voice","content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A voice is a sequence of musical events (e.g. notes, chords, rests) that proceeds linearly in time. The voice element is used to distinguish between multiple voices in individual parts. It is defined within a group due to its multiple uses within the MusicXML schema."}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"name":"staff","content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The staff element is defined within a group due to its use by both notes and direction elements."}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"name":"sound","content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"General playback parameters associated with this direction."}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"name":"listening","content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Specifies how a score-following or machine-listening application should interact with a performer, from this point in the performance onward."}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"name":"placement","content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The placement attribute indicates whether something is above or below another element, such as a note or a notation."}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"name":"isDirective","content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A Boolean value indicating whether this direction is a directive, changing its default horizontal position so its left-hand side aligns with the left-hand side of the time signature (or, if no time signature is present, the first music notational element in the measure). A default-x, justify, or halign attribute, if present, overrides this."}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"name":"system","content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The system-relation attribute group distinguishes elements that are associated with a system rather than the particular part where the element appears."}],"type":"paragraph"}]}]}],"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxldirection\/init(id:kind:offset:footnote:level:voice:staff:sound:listening:placement:isdirective:system:)"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"abstract":[{"text":"Creates a new ","type":"text"},{"code":"MXLDirection","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":".","type":"text"}],"kind":"symbol","metadata":{"title":"init(id:kind:offset:footnote:level:voice:staff:sound:listening:placement:isDirective:system:)","role":"symbol","modules":[{"name":"IvorMXL"}],"fragments":[{"text":"init","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"(","kind":"text"},{"text":"id","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"String","preciseIdentifier":"s:SS","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":"?, ","kind":"text"},{"text":"kind","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": [","kind":"text"},{"text":"Kind","preciseIdentifier":"s:7IvorMXL12MXLDirectionV4KindV","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":"], ","kind":"text"},{"text":"offset","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"MXLOffset","preciseIdentifier":"s:7IvorMXL9MXLOffsetV","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":"?, ","kind":"text"},{"text":"footnote","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"MXLFormattedText","preciseIdentifier":"s:7IvorMXL16MXLFormattedTextV","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":"?, ","kind":"text"},{"text":"level","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"MXLLevel","preciseIdentifier":"s:7IvorMXL8MXLLevelV","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":"?, ","kind":"text"},{"text":"voice","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"MXLVoice","preciseIdentifier":"s:7IvorMXL8MXLVoiceV","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":"?, ","kind":"text"},{"text":"staff","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"MXLStaff","preciseIdentifier":"s:7IvorMXL8MXLStaffV","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":"?, ","kind":"text"},{"text":"sound","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"MXLSound","preciseIdentifier":"s:7IvorMXL8MXLSoundV","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":"?, ","kind":"text"},{"text":"listening","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"MXLListening","preciseIdentifier":"s:7IvorMXL12MXLListeningV","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":"?, ","kind":"text"},{"text":"placement","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"MXLAboveBelow","preciseIdentifier":"s:7IvorMXL13MXLAboveBelowO","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":"?, ","kind":"text"},{"text":"isDirective","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Bool","preciseIdentifier":"s:Sb","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":"?, ","kind":"text"},{"text":"system","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"MXLSystemRelation","preciseIdentifier":"s:7IvorMXL17MXLSystemRelationO","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":"?)","kind":"text"}],"roleHeading":"Initializer","externalID":"s:7IvorMXL12MXLDirectionV2id4kind6offset8footnote5level5voice5staff5sound9listening9placement11isDirective6systemACSSSg_SayAC4KindVGAA9MXLOffsetVSgAA16MXLFormattedTextVSgAA8MXLLevelVSgAA8MXLVoiceVSgAA8MXLStaffVSgAA8MXLSoundVSgAA12MXLListeningVSgAA13MXLAboveBelowOSgSbSgAA17MXLSystemRelationOSgtcfc","symbolKind":"init"},"sections":[],"schemaVersion":{"minor":3,"patch":0,"major":0},"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL","doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLDirection"]]},"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLDirection\/init(id:kind:offset:footnote:level:voice:staff:sound:listening:placement:isDirective:system:)","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"references":{"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLVoice":{"url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlvoice","title":"MXLVoice","role":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"MXLVoice","kind":"identifier"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"text":"MXLVoice","kind":"identifier"}],"abstract":[{"text":"A voice is a sequence of musical events (e.g. notes, chords, rests) that proceeds linearly in time. The voice","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"element is used to distinguish between multiple voices in individual parts. It is defined within a group due","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"to its multiple uses within the MusicXML schema.","type":"text"}],"type":"topic","kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLVoice"},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLDirection":{"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"MXLDirection"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLDirection","title":"MXLDirection","kind":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"MXLDirection"}],"abstract":[{"text":"A direction is a musical indication that is not necessarily attached to a specific note. Two or more may be","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"text":"combined to indicate words followed by the start of a dashed line, the end of a wedge followed by dynamics,","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"text":"etc. For applications where a specific direction is indeed attached to a specific note, the direction element","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"text":"can be associated with the first note element that follows it in score order that is not in a different voice.","type":"text"}],"type":"topic","role":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxldirection"},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLOffset":{"type":"topic","role":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxloffset","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"An offset is represented in terms of divisions, and indicates where the direction will appear relative to the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"current musical location. The current musical location is always within the current measure, even at the end"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"of a measure."}],"navigatorTitle":[{"text":"MXLOffset","kind":"identifier"}],"kind":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"MXLOffset","kind":"identifier"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLOffset","title":"MXLOffset"},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLStaff":{"fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"MXLStaff","kind":"identifier"}],"kind":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"MXLStaff","kind":"identifier"}],"url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlstaff","role":"symbol","title":"MXLStaff","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLStaff","type":"topic","abstract":[{"text":"The staff element is defined within a group due to its use by both notes and direction elements.","type":"text"}]},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLSound":{"url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlsound","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"MXLSound"}],"title":"MXLSound","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLSound","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"MXLSound"}],"role":"symbol","type":"topic","kind":"symbol","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The sound element contains general playback parameters. They can stand alone within a part\/measure, or be a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"component element within a direction."}]},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLListening":{"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The listen and listening types, new in Version 4.0, specify different ways that a score following or machine"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"listening application can interact with a performer. The listening type handles interactions that change the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"state of the listening application from the specified point in the performance onward. If multiple child"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"elements of the same type are present, they should have distinct player and\/or time-only attributes."}],"role":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"MXLListening"}],"url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxllistening","kind":"symbol","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"MXLListening"}],"title":"MXLListening","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLListening","type":"topic"},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLAboveBelow":{"type":"topic","abstract":[{"text":"The above-below type is used to indicate whether one element appears above or below another element.","type":"text"}],"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"enum"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"MXLAboveBelow"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"MXLAboveBelow"}],"title":"MXLAboveBelow","kind":"symbol","role":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlabovebelow","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLAboveBelow"},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLSystemRelation":{"url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlsystemrelation","title":"MXLSystemRelation","role":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"enum","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"MXLSystemRelation","kind":"identifier"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"text":"MXLSystemRelation","kind":"identifier"}],"abstract":[{"text":"The system-relation type distinguishes elements that are associated with a system rather than the particular","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"part where the element appears. A value of only-top indicates that the element should appear only on the top","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"part of the current system. A value of also-top indicates that the element should appear on both the current","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"part and the top part of the current system. If this value appears in a score, when parts are created the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"element should only appear once in this part, not twice. A value of none indicates that the element is","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"associated only with the current part, not with the system.","type":"text"}],"type":"topic","kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLSystemRelation"},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLLevel":{"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"MXLLevel"}],"kind":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"MXLLevel"}],"url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxllevel","role":"symbol","title":"MXLLevel","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLLevel","type":"topic","abstract":[{"text":"The level type is used to specify editorial information for different MusicXML elements. The content contains","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"identifying and\/or descriptive text about the editorial status of the parent element.","type":"text"}]},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLDirection/init(id:kind:offset:footnote:level:voice:staff:sound:listening:placement:isDirective:system:)":{"url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxldirection\/init(id:kind:offset:footnote:level:voice:staff:sound:listening:placement:isdirective:system:)","title":"init(id:kind:offset:footnote:level:voice:staff:sound:listening:placement:isDirective:system:)","role":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"init","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"(","kind":"text"},{"text":"id","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"String","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:SS"},{"text":"?, ","kind":"text"},{"text":"kind","kin